   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 10 · Put THIS product into a scene (Krea 2 General Edit V2)\n**Use:** load a clean product shot (plain background) → describe the scene, call it \"the bag / shoe / bottle from the reference\nimage\" → Run → `S6/ref_product_*.png`. Turbo 8 steps, cfg 1, ref boost 2, new 4:5 canvas. \n**Why:** best detail fidelity on products in series 6 (bag: buckle, stitching, embossed fox emblem kept; sneaker: zigzag stripe).\n`10_ref_qwen21` is a close second and also takes a person + product together.\n- ref boost: 2 = new scene with the same product · 3–4 = closer copy of the product photo (may drag its lighting along).\n\n| Reference | Use | Why (series 6, 14 refs × 3 scenes) |\n|---|---|---|\n| object / product | **10_ref_product_krea** or 10_ref_qwen21 | emblem, buckle, stitching survive (DINOv2 bag 0.87 / 0.85) |\n| garment (print, embroidery) | **10_ref_qwen21** | koi embroidery + lemon print closest |\n| face / whole character | **10_ref_qwen21** | ArcFace 0.81–0.92 from ONE photo (our Maren LoRA: 0.55) — but it copies the photo's frontal pose |\n| new pose / new camera angle | **10_ref_klein** | re-stages naturally (sits, turns, walks); details a bit looser |\n| art style / film look | **10_ref_qwen21** | gouache, risograph, Cinestill look on new content |\n| place | 10_ref_qwen21 (same view) · 10_ref_klein (other viewpoint) | Qwen keeps the exact room, Klein can turn the camera |\n| palette / light only | **10_ref_style_krea** | Qwen and Qwen-Edit 2511 paste the reference picture as the background |\n| 2–3 references at once | **10_ref_qwen21**, toggles 2nd / 3rd | face + jacket + café all kept |"
   ]
  },
